{"name":"Lower Lip","hex":"#f7468a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lower lip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of labium inferius oris."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lower_lip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lip","blocks":[{"text":"The lips are a horizontal pair of soft appendages attached to the jaws and are the most visible part of the mouth of many animals, including humans. Mammal lips are soft, movable and serve to facilitate the ingestion of food and the articulation of sound and speech. Human lips are also a somatosensory organ, and can be an erogenous zone when used in kissing and other acts of intimacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Lips_2023.jpg/330px-Lips_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip","wikidata":"Q15173"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/MouthCupidBow.jpg/330px-MouthCupidBow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/MouthCupidBow.jpg/330px-MouthCupidBow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cupid's bow feature of a human lip","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMouthCupidBow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Adult_human_lips_anatomy_%28English%29.png/500px-Adult_human_lips_anatomy_%28English%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Adult_human_lips_anatomy_%28English%29.png/1280px-Adult_human_lips_anatomy_%28English%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Adult_human_lips_anatomy_%28English%29.png/500px-Adult_human_lips_anatomy_%28English